Here is the commit message:
SOLR-1095: fix stopword and keep filter performance issue

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/solr/trunk@761036 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by performance issues in the `StopFilterFactory` and `KeepWordFilterFactory`, which were using a generic `Set<String>` for storing words. This implementation was inefficient for lookups, leading to slower performance when processing tokens. The solution involved switching to `CharArraySet`, which is optimized for performance in such scenarios.

Here is the patch:
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.StopAnalyzer;
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.TokenStream;
